<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
    <!--
        CVE-2020-29582: Incorrect default permissions in kotlin-stdlib createTempDir/createTempFile.
        Fixed in Kotlin 1.4.21. Version 1.9.25 (transitive from Spring Boot) is not affected.
        The scanner matches on CPE regardless of the fix version, producing a false positive.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            False positive: CVE-2020-29582 was fixed in Kotlin 1.4.21.
            kotlin-stdlib 1.9.25 is not vulnerable.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/kotlin\-stdlib@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2020-29582</cve>
    </suppress>
    <!--
        CVE-2026-53914: Unsafe deserialization / code execution in the Kotlin compiler's
        build-cache metadata (fixed in Kotlin 2.4.20). Not applicable here: this is a Java
        library that ships kotlin-stdlib only as a transitive runtime dependency of okhttp;
        it does not run the Kotlin compiler or use the Kotlin build cache. The scanner matches
        on the jetbrains:kotlin CPE regardless of the affected component. Bumping is not an
        option because Kotlin 2.4.20 has no stable release yet (only 2.4.20-Beta*), and the
        project policy forbids pinning pre-releases.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Not applicable: CVE-2026-53914 affects the Kotlin compiler build cache, not the
            kotlin-stdlib runtime library pulled transitively by okhttp. No stable fix (2.4.20)
            is published yet.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/kotlin\-stdlib@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
    </suppress>
    <!--
        CVE-2022-31691: SnakeYAML deserialization reachable through the YAML editors in
        Spring Tools 4 for Eclipse (<= 4.16.1) and the VSCode extensions Spring Boot Tools,
        Concourse CI Pipeline Editor, Bosh Editor and Cloudfoundry Manifest YML Support
        (<= 1.40.0). Every affected product is an IDE or editor extension; none of them is
        org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-devtools, the Maven artifact scanned here.

        The match is a name collision followed by a version coincidence: the scanner reads
        "spring-boot-devtools" onto the vmware:spring_tools CPE, and Spring Boot's own 4.1.1
        happens to fall inside that IDE's "4.16.1 and below" range. It appeared the moment
        the parent moved to Boot 4 for that reason alone.

        No upgrade clears it, because no version of spring-boot-devtools was ever affected.
        4.1.1 is already the newest, matching the parent.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Not applicable: CVE-2022-31691 affects Spring Tools 4 for Eclipse and several
            VSCode extensions, not the spring-boot-devtools Maven artifact. Matched via the
            vmware:spring_tools CPE, whose "<= 4.16.1" range Spring Boot's 4.1.1 falls into
            by coincidence.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.boot/spring\-boot\-devtools@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2022-31691</cve>
    </suppress>
</suppressions>
